---
/**
 * Written against what the site actually does: three Netlify forms, Google
 * Analytics, Ahrefs, Userback, and the AxisCare hand-off. If a form field or a
 * third-party script changes, this page is the other half of that change.
 *
 * Deliberately absent: any claim of HIPAA compliance. A non-medical, private
 * pay agency is generally not a covered entity, and claiming to be one creates
 * an obligation that does not otherwise exist. The page says what is true —
 * health details are treated as confidential — without naming the statute.
 *
 * NOT REVIEWED BY COUNSEL. Marvalyn should have a lawyer read this before it
 * is relied on, particularly the referral section: that form takes health
 * information about a third party from someone who is not that person.
 */

// COMPONENTS
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";

// DATA
import { baseData, telHref, mailHref } from "@/data/siteData";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="September 8, 2026"
  pageTitle={`Privacy Policy | ${baseData.title}`}
  description="How Quantum Home Cares collects, uses, and protects the information you share through this website."
>
  <p class="lead">
    {baseData.legalName} respects the privacy of the families, professionals, and job applicants who contact
    us. This policy explains what this website collects, why, and what happens to it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <p>We only collect what you choose to send us. There are three forms on this site.</p>

  <h3>Care requests from families</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, phone number, email address, and whatever you tell us about the help you are looking
    for.
  </p>

  <h3>Referrals from professionals</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, organization, role, and contact details, along with the details you provide about the
    person you are referring. That can include their first name, their general location, the kind of
    support they need, and when care should start.
  </p>

  <h3>Job applications</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, contact details, the role you are applying for, the work history document you upload,
    and anything you write in the message box.
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Health information.</strong> A care request or a referral often includes details about someone's
      health or living situation. We treat that as confidential, share it only as described below, and
      ask that you send us only what we need in order to respond.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your request, usually within one business day.</li>
    <li>To assess whether we can take a case, and to plan care if we can.</li>
    <li>To evaluate job applicants and arrange interviews.</li>
    <li>To keep our own records of who contacted us and when.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    We do not sell your information. We do not rent or trade it. We do not use it to advertise to
    you, and we do not send marketing email to people who contacted us about care.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

  <p>
    We use a small number of service providers to run this website and our business. They only
    receive what they need to do their job.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts this website and processes form submissions.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>AxisCare</strong> is the client management system where care inquiries are recorded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics</strong> and <strong>Ahrefs</strong> tell us how the site is used.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Userback</strong> collects feedback about the website itself.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or where we believe someone is at risk
    of serious harm. Caregivers and staff see only what they need in order to provide care.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>

  <p>
    Our analytics tools use cookies and similar technology to count visits and understand which
    pages people read. This tells us about traffic patterns, not about you personally, and we do not
    use it to build a profile of you. Most browsers let you refuse cookies or delete them, and this
    site works without them.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>

  <p>
    We keep care inquiries and client records for as long as we are providing care and for a period
    afterward, so we can answer questions about the care that was given. Job applications are kept
    while the role is open and for a reasonable period after. Website analytics are retained on the
    schedule set by the analytics provider.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>

  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to us
    and we will respond. We may need to keep some records where the law or our own recordkeeping
    obligations require it, and we will tell you if that is the case.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This website is meant for adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you
    believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>

  <p>
    Form submissions travel over an encrypted connection, and access to what we store is limited to
    the people who need it. No website can promise perfect security, and we will not pretend
    otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    If this policy changes we will post the new version here and update the date at the top of the
    page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about this policy, or about information we hold, can go to <a href={mailHref}
      >{baseData.email}</a
    > or <a href={telHref}>{baseData.phone}</a>.
  </p>

  <p>{baseData.legalName} · {baseData.credentials.license}</p>
</LegalPage>
